<title>GERMANY: Kuehbacher says Italy won't join EMU without Prodi.</title>
<headline>Kuehbacher says Italy won't join EMU without Prodi.</headline>
<dateline>BERLIN 1997-05-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bundesbank council member Klaus-Dieter Kuehbacher said on Tuesday that Italy only has a chance to join Europe's planned monetary union from the start if Romano Prodi remains prime minister.</p>
<p>&quot;Only if Prodi remains head of government will Italy take part....if Prodi's government fails Italy has no chance at all to be in from the start.&quot;</p>
<p>The state central bank of Berlin and Brandenburg, of which Kuehbacher is president, confirmed that Kuehbacher made the remarks at a news conference.</p>
<p>Even if the current government remained in power it remained open whether Italy would fulfil the convergence critieria, Kuehbacher said.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
